[68.280, "o", "=== 2609.13761  (arxiv: 2609.13761)\r\n  title     : [2026-0912] [arXiv] Learning In-Hand Object Reaching to General 6D Poses   short: Learning In-Hand Object Reaching to General 6D Poses\r\n  authors   : Junxiao Lin, Tianyue Wu, Jie Yin ...\r\n  date      : 2026-09-12 <- arxiv:v1   venue: arXiv <- default\r\n  URL       : https://junxiaolin.github.io/poise-website/\r\n  PDF       : ok <- https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.13761\r\n  abstract  : In-hand manipulation allows multi-fingered dexterous hands to reconfigure grasped objects without releasing and regrasping them. This improves manipulation efficiency by reducing repeated grasp acquisition and large arm motions. However, most learning-based methods focus on reorientation, continuous...\r\n"]
[3.367, "o", "  collection: Dex-Manipulation\r\n  assign    : method:rl, embod:dex-hand\r\n      method:rl                <- abstract: ...In SE(3)), a sim-to-real reinforcement learning framework for this task....\r\n      method:rl                <- body x10: ...In SE(3)), a sim-to-real reinforcement learning framework for this task....\r\n      embod:dex-hand           <- abstract: ...allows multi-fingered dexterous hands to reconfigure grasped...\r\n      embod:dex-hand           <- body x4: ...allows multi-fingered dexterous hands to reconfigure grasped...\r\n  candidates: (not assigned — discuss with the user)\r\n      method:grasp-synthesis   3.5 weighted body hits, not in the abstract — could be related work or a baseline — the model agrees it applies  <- body x3: ...grasp synthesis paradigm...\r\n      embod:gripper            1.5 weighted body hits, not in the abstract — could be related work or a baseline  <- body x1: ...While parallel-jaw grippers are...\r\n      modality:vision          4 weighted body hits, not in the abstract — could be related work or a baseline — the model agrees it applies  <- body x4: ...RealSense D435 camera [42]....\r\n      modality:tactile         4 weighted body hits, not in the abstract — could be related work or a baseline — the model agrees it applies  <- body x3: ...adding tactile feedback, and...\r\n  model     : qwen3.5:9b (confidence 1.0) — The paper introduces POISE, a reinforcement learning framework for in-hand manipulation using multi-fingered dexterous hands (embod:dex-hand), which synthesizes stable grasps (method:grasp-synthesis) and utilizes RGB-D camera inputs (modality:vision) along with tactile feedback (modality:tactile).\r\n"]
